{
  "name": "CE-05 | Publish to YouTube",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CE-05 | Publish to YouTube Shorts\n**Trigger:** every 15 minutes.\n\n**Flow**\n1. Picks one row with `status = Publish` (you set this after watching the video). If `publish_at` has a date/time, it waits until then; blank = publish now.\n2. Daily cap: at most `maxPublishPerDay` uploads per day.\n3. Sets `Publishing`, downloads the final MP4 from Drive and uploads it with the **YouTube** node (title, description + \"#Shorts\" + AI disclosure line, tags).\n4. Writes `youtube_url` and `published_at`, status `Published`. If the upload fails the status becomes `Publish Failed` (set it back to `Publish` to retry).\n\n**Privacy:** uploads use `youtubePrivacy` from Config (default **private**). Projects that have not passed Google's YouTube API audit can usually only upload private videos anyway. Switch to `public` once you are ready.\n\n**AI label:** if your video looks realistic, YouTube asks you to disclose altered/synthetic content. The API node can't set that flag, so open the private video in YouTube Studio and set it before making it public.\n\n**Later:** TikTok / Instagram branches can be added here as extra nodes after *Download Final Video*.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 580,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "cfdba11e-5c6f-52ee-a3cd-e373aed4f74a",
      "name": "Note - How this works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -140
      ]
    },
